---
source: crates/escher-cli/tests/cli/usage.rs
expression: "long_help_snapshot(\"render-masks\")"
---
status: Success
--- stdout
Write one PNG mask for each colour of a colouring: the tile as a flat polygon in white, over which to paint the image fill of that colour for render, with each edge bordered in the same colour as every edge that it can meet in the tiling

Usage: escher render-masks [OPTIONS] --output <FILE> <SIGNATURE>

Arguments:
  <SIGNATURE>
          The signature in orbifold notation, such as *632. In a POSIX shell, put a signature that contains *, (, or ) in single quotes, as in '2*(12)'

Options:
  -o, --output <FILE>
          The file name from which the masks are named: mask.png gives mask-0.png, mask-1.png, and so on, one for each colour. Existing files are replaced

      --size <WIDTHxHEIGHT>
          The image size in pixels, as WIDTHxHEIGHT

          [default: 512x512]

      --colouring <COLOURING>
          One colour for every tile, parity for the colouring with two colours in which no two neighbouring tiles share a colour, or the id of a colouring that the command info --colourings lists, such as 4a. The default is parity when the tiling has it, and one otherwise

      --wythoff <MARKS>
          With --arrangement, write one mask of a polygon of a Wythoff construction for each picture, as three digits as for render, such as 010 for the heptagons of *732: for one picture to the --output file itself, for several pictures of one kind of polygon to files named as the masks of a colouring, mask-0.png for picture A, mask-1.png for B, and so on, and with several kinds of polygon to files named by the picture names that info --wythoff prints, such as mask-0A.png, mask-1A.png, and mask-1B.png

      --arrangement <ID>
          With --wythoff on a regular tiling or a tiling with several kinds of polygon, border each edge of the mask of each picture to show how it meets its neighbour in the arrangement with this id, such as 12a, which the command info --wythoff lists

      --set <NAME=VALUE>
          Set a shape parameter, as NAME=VALUE, such as aspect=1.5.

          A shape parameter is a number that changes the shape of the tiles without
          changing their symmetry. Which parameters exist depends on the signature:

            aspect
                The ratio of the sides of the rectangle or the parallelogram, for
                *2222, 2222, o, **, xx, *x, 22*, 22x, and 2*22.
            skew
                The shear of the parallelogram of o and of the two rectangles of 2222.
            cornerpair<k>.length
                For a hyperbolic reflection polygon *p1...pn with 4 to 8 corners, the
                length of the side between the two right angles of its k-th pair of
                adjacent corners of order 2.
            slice<i>.length
                For the same polygons, the length of the i-th cut across the polygon,
                a common perpendicular of two of its sides. A polygon with n corners
                has n - 3 lengths, corner pairs first.

          Every other signature has no shape parameter. escher info <SIGNATURE>
          prints one Parameter line for each parameter of the signature, with its
          range and default.

          Give the option once for each parameter, as in:

            escher render o --set aspect=2 --set skew=0.25 -o /tmp/torus.png
            escher render '*3333' --set slice1.length=2 -o /tmp/square.png

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
--- stderr
--- end
